"QNet" means the Minecraft mod QNet in every version and form in which cptgummiball publishes it:
the jar files, the compiled code in them, textures, models, icons, sounds, texts, language files,
data files and documentation, and the QNet API files (section 5).

1. Ownership
   QNet is the property of cptgummiball. This license gives you limited rights to use it. It does
   not transfer any ownership, copyright or other rights. All rights not expressly granted here are
   reserved.

2. What you may do
   a) Download QNet from its official pages (Modrinth, CurseForge, and the releases of
      https://github.com/CptGummiball/QNet).
   b) Use QNet to play Minecraft: in singleplayer, and on your own or any other server.
   c) Show QNet in videos, streams, screenshots, reviews and guides.

3. Modpacks
   You may include QNet in modpacks, public or private, free or paid, and distribute it as part of
   such a modpack, but only in its original, unmodified state: the jar files exactly as
   cptgummiball published them, not renamed in content, not repackaged, not altered in any way.
   Where the modpack platform can link to the official download instead of copying the file,
   linking is preferred.

4. What you may not do
   Unless cptgummiball has given you written permission, you may not:
   a) modify, adapt, translate, patch or otherwise change QNet or any part of it, or create works
      derived from it, including modified jar files, forks, ports and re-textures;
   b) decompile, disassemble, deobfuscate or otherwise reverse engineer QNet, or attempt to obtain
      its source code, except where and only to the extent that applicable law expressly allows
      this despite this restriction;
   c) upload, mirror or distribute QNet anywhere other than as part of a modpack under section 3,
      or offer it as your own work;
   d) use the textures, models, icons, sounds or texts of QNet in other projects;
   e) remove or change this license or any copyright notice.

5. QNet API
   cptgummiball publishes an API for other mods: the Java package dev.cptgummiball.qnet.api
   (provided as a separate API jar with its documentation) and the documented integration classes,
   if any. You may use the API jar, the documentation and the official QNet jar files as
   compile-only dependencies to develop, compile and distribute your own mods that work together
   with QNet. Your mod may reference these classes, but must not contain the API classes or any
   other part of QNet; players install QNet separately. The API may not be modified or
   redistributed on its own. Sections 1 and 4 apply to the API in all other respects.

6. Pipster
   QNet requires the separate mod Pipster. Pipster is not part of QNet and is not covered by this
   license; it has its own license (the Pipster License) and its own official pages. Players and
   modpacks install Pipster separately, under the terms of the Pipster License.

7. Earlier mods
   QNet continues the mods QuantaWorks, QuantaVolt and QuantaRift by cptgummiball. Versions
   published under those names remain under their own licenses. This license applies to
   everything published under the name QNet, including content that first appeared in those mods.

8. No warranty
   QNet is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including
   warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. Back up
   your worlds, in particular before converting a world from QuantaWorks, QuantaVolt or QuantaRift
   to QNet.

9. Limitation of liability
   To the extent permitted by applicable law, cptgummiball is not liable for any damages arising
   from the use of or inability to use QNet, including loss of data or of game worlds. Liability
